# Prime Number Finder Release Notes

## 1.0.0 (25 Mar 2025)

### New Features

- Initial release

## 1.0.1 (25 Mar 2025)

### Improvements

- General maintenance and minor patches

## 1.0.2 (25 Mar 2025)

### Improvements

- General maintenance and minor patches

## 1.1.0 (26 Mar 2025)

### Improvements

- Cleaned up the semiprime and squarefree prime checks

### Documentation

- Added docstrings to each function in `prime_checker` to make it more apparent what's going on

## 1.2.1 (27 Mar 2025)

### Improvements

- Broke out `digit_sum` function to two separate functions for logic cleanup purposes

### Bug Fixes

- Moved calculations to check functions and out of the `prime_check` function

## 1.5.0 (31 Mar 2025)

### New Features

- Added toggle button for light/dark themes
- Updated check input box to be able to have text in it as well so the `check_output` widget could go away

### Improvements

- Updated UI to be more in line with other apps

## 1.7.0 (01 Apr 2025)

### Improvements

- Moved `current_number.txt` and `prime_numbers.txt` file into new `resources/data` directory
- Deleted unused `config_handler.py` and combined `prime_file_handler.py` and `yaml_file_handler.py` into one `file_handler.py` file

## 1.7.1 (01 Apr 2025)

### Improvements

- Deleted unused `config_handler.py` file

## 1.8.0 (02 Apr 2025)

### Improvements

- Switched from using `.TXT` files for data storage to using a sqlite3 database

## 1.8.1 (31 Oct 2025)

### Improvements

- Reduced required Python version to 3.10

## 1.8.2 (23 Jun 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies

## 1.8.3 (21 Jul 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies

## 1.8.17 (26 Oct 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies and Python versions

## 2.0.0 (20 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added a modern card-based UI layout with dedicated sections for stats and number checks
- Added a complete overhaul of the theming system, introducing custom "Prime Number Finder Dark/Light" palettes alongside Phaino, Equinox, Catppuccin, Solarized, and Gruvbox themes
- Added a Preferences dialog to live-switch themes and manage settings
- Added an About dialog accessible from the Help menu
- Added a "Copy Most Recent Prime" action to the Edit menu
- Added visual feedback for primality checks (green for Prime, red for Not Prime) and clipboard copies in the result label
- The manual check input now supports arbitrarily large integers (removed the 32-bit limitation)

### Improvements

- Moved user data (database and settings) to `~/.config/prime_number_finder/` to keep the virtual environment clean and persist data across uninstalls
- Refactored `app.py` to extract UI generation into a dedicated `ui_manager.py` component
- Cleaned up dead code and removed legacy terminal/CLI logic from `prime_checker.py`
- Removed the backup/restore database functionality from `install.py` as the `.config` directory now handles persistence natively
- Updated `install.py` to be completely project-agnostic and accept the package name as an argument
- Pressing Enter in the manual check input field now triggers the check action
- Set minimum window size to prevent UI elements from squishing on smaller screens

## 2.1.0 (23 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added the "Sugar Pop" (light) and "Sugar Goth" (dark) themes to the theme selection.

### Improvements

- **Ecosystem Unification:** Standardized the `ThemeManager`, `themes.yaml`, and `styles.qss` across all Melvin Quick applications for a consistent cross-app experience.
- Removed all one-off app-specific themes (e.g., Prime Number Finder Dark/Light) in favor of shared ecosystem themes.
- Renamed the legacy "Phaino Dark/Light" themes to "Phaino Dusk" and "Phaino Dawn".
- Simplified the theme sorting logic in the Preferences dialog to automatically group Dark/Dusk themes before Light/Dawn themes, and alphabetize the list.
- Updated the default theme to "Sugar Goth".

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed an issue where the Preferences dialog would not update its own styling when a new theme was selected.
